## 3. Decisions Made & Constraints
**CLAUDE.md working rules:**
- Plan mode at each phase start.
- Ask before any schema / permission / tenant-isolation / token-content change.
- Tests with every feature; never commit secrets.
- A dated Status note after each phase.
- Stop and ask on a conflict with CLAUDE.md.

**Never:**
- put a JWT in a URL
- trust tile-hiding as access control
- make customer forks
- deploy dev-module
- ask the user to paste passwords
- print `.env` values
- let an app import another app (shared code only via `packages/*`)

**Tokens:**
- SSO token is unchanged.
- Summary token: `purpose:"summary"`.
- **Support token** (built): `purpose:"support"`, tenant_id, super_admin_id, `read_only:true`, aud, 15 min. It
  carries no name; owner logs say "PlantOps support".

**Lab Records decisions:**
- FSSAI Forms 1–4 + daily test log.
- **Append-only**: save = submit + lock, no drafts; correction = new version with a reason (DB check);
  retest = new entry; `lab_app` has no UPDATE / DELETE on result tables.
- Limits are copied into each result.
- **lab_lead** (approve / release / reject / verify / set limits) + owner (same, plus export; no data entry).
- Batch status pending / on_hold / approved / **rejected** (final).
- **"Still failing" is judged per parameter by the most recent result on the batch.**
- **Print-ready HTML pages, not Puppeteer.**
- History window by plan (hidden, never deleted).
- Search inside the module.
- Form 1 "tested at" (in-house / outside lab) + "Form 1 due".
- WhatsApp outbox to owners + lab leads.
- Daily reminder for holds > 24 h.

**Document Store decisions:**
- **Email** reminders (SMTP).
- Responsible = a plant user (owner or document_keeper).
- **Renewal keeps history.**
- Reminders at 30 / 7 / 1 / 0 days (0 also covers 1–6 days after expiry), then weekly; unique
  `(version_id, stage, recipient_user_id)`; one email per person per run.
- Files: PDF / JPEG / PNG / WebP by magic bytes, ≤ 10 MB, plan `storage_mb`.

**Redirect rule:** module callbacks use a **relative Location**. `req.url` is `0.0.0.0` in phone mode.

